join Lindi (Neutral) left
join Hope (Neutral) right
update Lindi (Warm)
Lindi: Three people asked me today what's still good to gather. Not 'is there anything' — what.
- That's different?
	Hope: That's different?
	Lindi: Completely different. 'Is there anything' is a question you ask when you're frightened.
	Lindi: 'What' is a question you ask when you're planning.
Lindi: Half of what I told them came from Mama Zulu. The roots, mostly — I'd never have found those on my own and I've got them written down now in about four places so they don't go anywhere.
- She'd be pleased
	Hope: She'd be pleased.
	Lindi: She knows. I've told her. She said 'mm,' which from her is a parade.
Lindi: This is the part I'd have written up, if I'd finished. Four years of survey and a hunger gap nobody's afraid of.
Lindi: Anyway. There's a rack that needs turning.
[signal arg="hearts:lindi:1"]
set {GameState.lindi_epilogue_scene_complete} = true
